{
  "_about": "Handle moderation (backend/moderation.py, mirrored in frontend/src/moderation/handle.js). Matched on the lowercased handle after leetspeak is undone and underscores are removed; every letter may repeat (fuuuck). 'anywhere' terms match inside longer handles; 'whole' terms collide with ordinary words (spicy, raccoon), so they only match a whole handle or one underscore-separated part. 'targets' x 'insults' catches hateful pairs in either order (whitepig, pig_white). 'allow' words are blanked out first, so grapefruit or therapist pass. Keep the frontend copy identical: tests/test_moderation.py checks it. 'allow' is applied longest-first, so grapefruit wins over grape. Religious figures, extremists and brand names (god, allah, jesus, satan, osama, hitler, twitter, nutella...) were added in v1.0.1 at the owner's request; 'exact' terms match a whole handle or one underscore part exactly, with no repeated letters (g+o+d+ would also hit good). v1.0.2: terrorist and extremist names and groups added (al qaeda, isis/isil, boko haram, al shabaab, hamas, hezbollah, taliban, unabomber, mcveigh, breivik, tarrant, ku klux, gestapo, auschwitz). 'transpose' terms also block every one-swap typo of themselves (adlof, htiler, osmaa): swaps of terms 6+ letters long match anywhere, shorter ones only a whole handle or one underscore part, so 'astan' (a satan swap) doesn't catch astana. isil and tarrant are 'whole' because they hide inside missile-like words and a common surname.",
